WEBVTT

00:01:29.685 --> 00:01:31.789
Susan Cain, welcome.

00:01:31.813 --> 00:01:34.072
SC: Thank you so much.
It's great to be here.

00:01:34.096 --> 00:01:36.519
CA: We’re very excited to have you here.

00:01:36.543 --> 00:01:38.017
You’re a revolutionary.

00:01:38.041 --> 00:01:41.188
Honestly, you’ve ushered in
this revolution.

00:01:41.212 --> 00:01:42.534
I think we can say that,

00:01:42.558 --> 00:01:46.931
because not many people do
anything like you have done.

00:01:46.955 --> 00:01:50.510
So, introversion-extroversion:
let's talk some science.

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:53.876
I'd love to hear
your definition, fundamentally,

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.063
of how we should think about
what an introvert is versus an extrovert.

00:01:58.087 --> 00:02:01.034
SC: The one-minute answer:
you could ask yourself